 "summary": "Purine nucleotides are broken down to free bases and then to uric acid (xanthine oxidase), or the bases are salvaged back to nucleotides with PRPP (HGPRT for hypoxanthine and guanine, APRT for adenine). Clinical: SCID (ADA deficiency), Lesch-Nyhan (no HGPRT), gout and tumor lysis (↑ uric acid; allopurinol, febuxostat inhibit xanthine oxidase).",
